    "done_when": "One function reads the committed ledger rows and the live pointers, matches each run to its plan by plan, then plan_link, then the plan its node id names (a plan review's node id, which ends in the plan's slug, and a run review through the run it reviews), and returns per plan the dispatching session of the most recent matching run inside a configured staleness window, its tier (coordinator or unowned), whether that session is live, and the plan's plan-owner beside it. On a fixture built from power_convertor's committed ledger, shared-coil-supply-model, iter-switched-terminal-transients and tf-co-wound-tape-validation each resolve to the session the test pins as a literal read from the fixture rows by hand, and the gate log names the deciding row and matched field for each; a plan with no rows resolves to unowned. A plan dispatched by session A then session B resolves to B. Negative controls: a resolver returning unowned for every plan fails the fixture test, and one ignoring dispatch order fails the A-then-B test. On the base commit the function does not exist, so the test fails there. Gate: tests/test_a_plans_coordinator_is_derived_from_the_ledger.py tests/test_crew_obligations.py tests/test_ledger.py tests/test_every_module_fits_a_worker_window.py. Run the gate in the foreground on the fleet allocation, with the revision, tree and command on the log's first line; ruff check and ruff format --check report nothing added on the staged paths.",
